WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.936
-Thank you so much for being
in studio, for being here.

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:07.339
-Nah, when I got the offer...
-Yeah.

00:00:07.339 --> 00:00:10.709
-...I said, especially MLK Day,

00:00:10.709 --> 00:00:12.612
I'm gonna come here in person
to be with you.

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:14.080
-Thank you for that.
I appreciate that.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.081
Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:16.349
Means a lot.
Thank you.

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:18.584
-Thank you, thank you.
-I appreciate that.

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:22.388
I want to get into
"Da 5 Bloods."

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:25.158
You know I loved it.
-Thank you very much.

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:27.427
Second time for "Da 5 Bloods,"
appreciate it.

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:30.896
-Yeah, that's right.
I want to talk to you about

00:00:30.896 --> 00:00:33.165
a project I heard is going to be
your next project.

00:00:33.165 --> 00:00:36.035
-Right.
-Stop me if I'm wrong.

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:38.537
It's a musical, right?
Okay?

00:00:38.537 --> 00:00:42.708
You're doing a musical,
and it's a musical about Viagra.

00:00:42.708 --> 00:00:45.211
-True story.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:48.080
And I'd like to say, though,

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:50.249
if God willing,
and the creek doesn't rise.

00:00:50.249 --> 00:00:52.318
But I want to give you
another piece of information

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:57.857
about the film referred to,
Brother Jimmy.

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:59.025
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:01.226
This is gonna be
the hardest film I ever made.

00:01:01.226 --> 00:01:05.531
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:09.335
♪♪

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.871
I had to think of all --
-Had to think of all of it --

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:13.673
-It's gonna be the hardest film
I ever made!

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:16.308
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.308 --> 00:01:18.678
Stop the show! Stop the show!
-Stop the show!

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:21.347
Go to commercial!
Go to commercial!

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:23.683
-I want to talk about
your other film,

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:25.985
the one that you came out
before, "Da 5 Bloods."

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:28.888
-Yes.
-It is on every list

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:33.226
for award buzz.
And well-deserved.

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:36.328
I loved it. And I actually
told you, my dad was in Vietnam,

00:01:36.328 --> 00:01:38.631
and I had him --
-You told me that.

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:42.769
-Dude, he loved it, as well.
I just love that all these guys

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:49.175
and girls have stories to tell
that fought in Vietnam.

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:54.747
-Well, again, thank you for
having me today, on MLK Day.

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:58.218
The black soldiers in Vietnam
did not know

00:01:58.218 --> 00:02:01.321
till two or three days later

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:04.957
that Dr. King
had been assassinated.

00:02:04.957 --> 00:02:07.994
And, uh...

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:11.698
They learned
through Hanoi Hannah...

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:12.765
-Yeah.

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:16.669
-...who was the voice
of the Viet Cong.

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:20.373
Hanoi Hannah
told the black soldiers,

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:25.411
"Why are you fighting for a
country that does not love you?

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:27.780
Why are you fighting
for this country

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.984
when your brothers and sisters

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:34.720
are burning
a hundred cities in America?"

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:36.856
And that's documented.

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:41.460
And to continue this,
April 4, 1968,

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:45.331
I was 11 years old.

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:49.402
11 years old,
sitting on my stoop --

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:51.870
Not porch!
In Brooklyn, it's stoops.

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:53.939
-Yep, that's right.
-Stoops!

00:02:53.939 --> 00:02:57.276
I hear a woman screaming.

00:02:57.276 --> 00:02:59.846
And as the voice gets closer,

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:03.215
I recognize,
it's my mother's voice.

00:03:03.215 --> 00:03:06.218
And she's screaming --
I swear on her grave --

00:03:06.218 --> 00:03:10.690
She's screaming,
"They killed Dr. King!

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:14.427
They killed Dr. King!
They killed Dr. King!"

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:19.699
And an argument can be made that
Dr. King was assassinated

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:21.434
not because of
the Civil Rights Movement

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:26.372
but because he was one of
the first people, vocally,

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:30.342
out front, to say the war
in Vietnam was immoral.

00:03:30.342 --> 00:03:33.813
-That scene in the movie
is so poignant

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:36.916
because they're hearing this
over the radio.

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:38.818
-That's where the majority
of the black troops --

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:44.757
Would also like to say, in the
latest stage of the Vietnam War,

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:47.326
black soldiers, the Bloods,

00:03:47.326 --> 00:03:50.262
they made up a third
of the fighting forces.

00:03:50.262 --> 00:03:54.634
Yet African-Americans
are only 10% of the population

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:56.302
of the United States of America.

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:58.737
Only 10% of the population
but yet we were third

00:03:58.737 --> 00:04:00.940
of the fighting force
in Vietnam.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:03.275
Facts.
Facts, undisputable.

00:04:03.275 --> 00:04:04.811
-I'm glad you're
getting it out there,

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:07.113
because these stories
need to be heard.

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:11.284
-Yeah, there's so many stories.
And also, over the years,

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:13.319
thank you for having me
on your show,

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:16.054
letting me reach your audience,
love.

00:04:16.054 --> 00:04:17.991
The Roots, love you guys.

00:04:17.991 --> 00:04:19.959
The Knicks are good this year.
Watch me.

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:22.929
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.929 --> 00:04:25.365
-I want to show everyone
a clip from the movie.

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:27.399
Here is a scene
from "Da 5 Bloods."

00:04:27.399 --> 00:04:29.435
Take a look at this.

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:33.873
-Black G.I.
In Memphis, Tennessee,

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:37.877
a white man assassinate
Dr. Martin Luther King.

00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:44.350
Dr. King also opposed
the U.S. War in Vietnam.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:50.289 line:0%
Black G.I., your government
sent 600,000 troops

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:52.525 line:0%
to crush the rebellion.

00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:55.794 line:0%
Your soul sister
and soul brothers

00:04:55.794 --> 00:04:59.932 line:0%
are enraged in over 122 cities.

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:01.700 line:0%
They kill them.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:04.003 line:0%
Why you fight against us?

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:08.841
So far away
from where you are needed.

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:10.743
[ Applause ]

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:13.379
-Spike Lee, everybody,
the one and only!

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:15.180
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:16.249
You know I love you, man.

00:05:16.249 --> 00:05:19.151
Thank you so much
for being here in studio.

00:05:19.151 --> 00:05:21.254
-The house!
-Spike Lee.

00:05:21.254 --> 00:05:23.723
"Da 5 Bloods"
is streaming now on Netflix.

